Well, then where's the musical instrument that the Mule used to enhance
his emotional control?  (What was the instrument called?)
You strum on your harp...   The Troll becomes depressed -more-
The Troll dies.
                  -or-
You strum on your harp -more-
The mountain nymph is REALLY friendly -more-
The mountain nymph gives you all her possessions.
                  -or-
You strum on your harp...   The succubus becomes...

There seems to be an infinite number of possibilities like this.  Has
the dev team (whoever you are) ever considered making nethack easily
re-configurable, so anyone can create their own little universe and
experiment with game balance?  Mainly, all the various structures should
have configuration files which are easy to deal with (C structures nested
3 deep are not easy to deal with unless you wrote the code).  You would
also want it to provide lot's of hooks for easily adding custom pieces
of code (like the code for a sword of create monster).  I think
the dev team should think about going in this direction in the long
term.

I do want one small feature added to the user interface:  an option to
turn off the listing of objects where you are (especially when you are
blind).  To move down a corridor filled with stuff I have to type:
    h-spc-spc-spc-h-spc-spc-spc-h-spc-spc-spc
All those space bars get old real quick.  I would be happy just to be told
that there is something there.  If I want to look at it, I can hit ':'
If I don't want to look at it, then I never need to touch the space bar.

